===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{tennis}} To play a soft drop shot.
# {{football}} To [[chip]] lightly, to play a light [[chip]] shot.
#: ''The forward '''dinked''' the ball over the goalkeeper to score his first goal of the season.''
#* {{quote-news
|year=2010
|date=December 28
|author=Kevin Darlin
|title=West Brom 1 - 3 Blackburn
|work=BBC
|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport1/hi/football/eng_prem/9308862.stm
|page=
|passage=But the visitors started the game in stunning fashion when Morten Gamst Pedersen '''dinked''' forward a clever looping pass and Kalinic beat the offside trap, surged into the box and beautifully placed the ball past goalkeeper Scott Carson.}}
# {{Australia|colloquial}} To carry someone on a pushbike: behind, on the crossbar or on the handlebar.
#: ''I gave him a '''dink''' on my bike.''
#* '''1947''', [[w:John Lehmann|John Lehmann]] (editor), ''The Penguin New Writing'', Issue 30, [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=z9EzAAAAMAAJ&q=bicycle+%22dink%22&dq=bicycle+%22dink%22&hl=en&ei=ereATbXSB82qcbWd2P4G&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=66&ved=0COECEOgBMEE page 103],
#*: I didn't like them at all ; only the lame one who used to let me '''dink''' him home on his bicycle.

